From 950620b8aba38f6d4a3e3bb7051263b7d95d058f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:09:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): retain artifact-keyed author custody across
 rework runs [daveey]

Tie concrete PR-head authorship to delivered artifact identities, not verdict boundaries. Retain authors through continued/crashed/no-spawn rework and A-to-B-to-A returns. Complete review_commit_range receipts permit release only for disjoint commit sets; missing range receipts conservatively retain earlier heads of the same PR. Open and merged head identities are supported. Artifact-less historical handoffs preserve the legacy fallback; downstream source provenance stays full-history.

Proof: 17 consumer files, 490 tests passed. scripts/check passes. Eight new lifecycle probes are red with artifact custody disabled; disjoint-range regression red before range support. Eight source mutants killed against a green 96-test baseline. Exact-head CI and independent review remain required before canonical ship.
